course: dictionary
lesson: 914
title: Blame and responsibility
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To blame someone means to say or think that they caused something bad. «Blaming others for your mistake is unfair, and people stop trusting you.» Here, blaming means pointing at someone else as the cause of your own wrong.
explain: The blame is the responsibility for something bad that happened. If a vase breaks and you say your brother did it, you are putting the blame on him. Before you blame anyone, ask: who really caused it?
explain: «To be to blame» means to be the one who caused it. «In a game of chance nobody is to blame for losing» because luck decides the result, not a person's action.
fact: Blame can be a verb, as in «I blame the wet grass», or a noun, as in «the blame is mine».
fact: The verb changes its ending: blame, blames, blamed, blaming.
fact: «Blame» means to say or think that someone caused something bad.
fact: «To be to blame» means to be the one who caused it.
fact: «Put the blame on» means to say that someone else caused the problem.
exercise: «Blaming others for your mistake is unfair, and people stop trusting you.» What does blaming mean here? | *Saying someone else caused your bad mistake | Running very fast | Giving someone a present | Forgetting something important
exercise: «In a game of chance nobody is to blame for losing.» Why is nobody to blame? | Everyone cheated | The loser was too slow | Players were too noisy | *Luck decides the result, not a person's action
exercise: Which phrase means to be the one who caused it? | To be on time | To be quick | *To be to blame | To be hungry
test: Mia breaks the window and says her little brother did it. What is she doing? | Clearing her name in front of everyone | *Blaming someone else for her own mistake | Taking the blame bravely | Telling a joke
test: «Clearing the name of the person you blamed, in front of the same people, is part of putting it right.» What should you do to put things right? | *Clear the name of the person you wrongly blamed, in front of the same people | Hide from the people | Blame someone else again | Say sorry to nobody
exam: Which sentence uses blame as a noun meaning responsibility? | We are blaming the referee | I blame the wind for the broken kite | *The blame for the broken kite is mine | She blamed the dog for the mess
